From: Paul Praschl <praschlpaul@g-p.at>
Date: Tue, 14 Jul 2026 15:55:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 006/117] dt-bindings: clock: Apple T8010 touch clock

The T8010 PMGR contains a dedicated clock gate and integer divider for the
touch controller.  The block uses clkref as its parent and exposes enable,
busy and divider fields through a PMGR register pair.

Describe the block as a single-output clock provider.  Require its PMGR
register range, parent clock and target clock-frequency, and allow it as a
child of the Apple PMGR syscon.

This binding only describes the clock hardware; the consumer and provider
driver are added separately.  The schema passes dt-doc-validate.  The full
series was boot-tested on J172 with a 24 MHz touch clock.

Signed-off-by: Paul Praschl <praschlpaul@g-p.at>

Orchard-replay-of: f5d472c587f24b29f2cbcce8ad0d796c0e8cfb09
